# Documentation with code changes

When you edit **`src/`** (or `README.md` / `AGENTS.md` / `docs/module-map/`), finish the task only after updating docs **if the change would make them wrong or incomplete**.

1. **`docs/module-map/<module>.md`** — Update the module you touched (commands, handlers, managers, flows, **`customId`** prefixes from `src/lib/constants/custom-ids.ts`). Update multiple module files if shared `src/lib/` code affects them.
2. **`README.md`** — If install steps, config, or overview text should change, update it.

Do **not** recreate `docs/module-plans/`; that folder was removed. Prefer concise updates to **`docs/module-map/`** over new standalone planning docs.

Read **`AGENTS.md`** for layout, `enabledModules`, and conventions.
